  "comment": "Every input jack is read with getVoltage(), so nothing here is polyphonic on the way in; TRAIT and MASS are the only polyphonic outputs and always carry exactly eight channels in habitat order. The TRAIT channels follow an occupancy latch rather than the raw local mean: a channel stops updating when its habitat's mass crosses the extinction threshold and picks up again from the newly established mean on colonisation, so a dying voice holds its pitch instead of falling to 0V. The panel numbers habitats 1 to 8 while the equations index them from zero, so the barrier the manual calls the 4-5 link is between the fourth and fifth panel habitats."
